title: "The Primacy Premium: conditional forecasts of defense and commercial markets under Chinese military primacy, 2026 to 2035"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agard
    given-names: Alyssa I.
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alyssaagard/primacy-premium"
url: "https://primacy.alyssaagard.dev/"
keywords:
  - defense economics
  - defense policy
  - conditional forecasting
  - uncertainty propagation
  - reserve currencies
  - arms transfers
  - military expenditure
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A seeded Python pipeline that estimates response parameters from IMF and
  SIPRI data and simulates three pathways to Chinese military primacy by 2035
  (accretion, retrenchment, demonstration). It tests whether allied defense
  expenditure and reserve currency composition depend on the pathway. The
  repository contains the parsers, estimation and simulation code, processed
  tables, a hypothesis dataset, an interactive results page, and a report.
